            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a continent, then the Arabic for a volcano."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: سبب",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سبب — sabab — \"a reason, a cause\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سبب (sabab) is built on the native Arabic root s-b-b, \"a rope; a means\" (Lane). Lane's sabab is a rope by which one reaches a thing, hence a means, a cause."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
